---
source: crates/web/src/tests.rs
expression: "readable(&f, card_of(&ask.body))"
---
<div class="cf">
<p class="kind">Agent</p>
<h1>Revise this review?</h1>
<div class="who">
<div class="t">Add the thing</div>
<div class="m">
<a class="ref" href="https://github.com/org/repo/pull/7" title="https://github.com/org/repo/pull/7">org/repo#7 ↗</a> · alice · run 1, reviewed <code>head7</code>
</div>
<ul class="explain">
<li>It resumes run 1's agent session, not interactively, with your instruction.</li>
<li>The result is a new run with a fresh set of drafts for the same reviewed commit, <code>head7</code>.</li>
<li>This run and its drafts, your edits included, stay as they are. The agent sees them, and keeps your accepted and edited drafts unless you ask otherwise; ones it keeps word for word stay accepted.</li>
<li>It's refused if the PR has moved on since this review: start a fresh review instead.</li>
</ul>
<label class="instruction" for="instruction">Your instruction</label>
<textarea id="instruction" form="confirm" name="instruction" rows="4" required autofocus placeholder="e.g. Drop the nits, and say more about the error handling.">
</textarea>
</div>
<p class="cost">Spends tokens: the agent works again, with your instruction.</p>
<div class="btns">
<form id="confirm" method="post" action="/pr/org/repo/7/runs/1/regenerate">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<token>">
<button class="btn go" type="submit">Revise the review<span class="k">y</span>
</button>
</form>
<a class="btn" id="cancel" href="/pr/org/repo/7?run=1">Cancel<span class="k">Esc</span>
</a>
</div>
</div>
